# AI Governance Practice — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Never commit real values;
# `.gitignore` covers `.env.local` and everything else matching `.env*`.
#
# All variables are OPTIONAL. With none of them set the app runs in local mode:
# every feature works and progress is saved in the browser. Adding Supabase
# credentials turns on accounts and cross-device sync.
#
# NOTE: every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the client bundle at BUILD
# time, not read at runtime. Changing one in Vercel requires a redeploy to take
# effect, and none of them may hold a secret.

# --- Supabase (optional: enables auth + progress sync) ----------------------
# Project Settings → API keys in the Supabase dashboard.
#
# The key is the publishable / anon key — the one intended to reach browsers.
# Both formats work: the current `sb_publishable_...` format and the legacy
# `eyJ...` anon JWT. Never put the service role or secret key here; it would be
# inlined into the client bundle and readable by anyone.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# --- Auth redirect ----------------------------------------------------------
# Where Supabase email-confirmation links return the user. No trailing slash;
# the app appends `/login`.
#
# Required in production. Without it, confirmation links fall back to the
# Supabase project's default Site URL, and the mobile build has no window
# origin to fall back to at all.
#
# Must also be registered in Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration ->
# Redirect URLs, or Supabase rejects the redirect.
#   local:  http://localhost:3000
#   Vercel: https://your-domain.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.vercel.app

# --- Starring the project on GitHub (optional) ------------------------------
# Turns on the "Star this project" control in Settings. Leave either value
# unset and the control does not render at all — a button that cannot work is
# worse than no button.
#
# The client id is public by design; the client *secret* is not and must never
# appear here, because every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the browser
# bundle at build time. The secret lives in the Edge Function's own secrets.
#
# Setup:
#   1. GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> OAuth Apps -> New OAuth App
#      Authorization callback URL: https://<your-domain>/github/callback
#   2. supabase functions deploy github-oauth --no-verify-jwt
#   3. supabase secrets set GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=... GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=... \
#        ALLOWED_ORIGINS="https://<your-domain>,capacitor://localhost,https://localhost"
#   4. Set the two variables below and redeploy, since both are build-time
#      inlined and a dashboard change alone does nothing.
#
# SCOPE. Starring requires `public_repo`, which is the narrowest scope GitHub
# offers for it and still grants write access to the user's public
# repositories. The consent screen will say so. The app states it before
# sending anyone there, and works identically for anyone who declines.
#
# This flow is deliberately independent of Supabase Auth. Using Supabase's
# GitHub provider would replace the current session, signing a learner out of
# the account holding their progress; starring a repository must not be able to
# cost someone their study history.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_OAUTH_ENDPOINT=

# --- Seeding only (server-side; never expose to the client) -----------------
# Used by `npm run seed` to write the question bank into the database.
# Deliberately has no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so it is never inlined into the
# browser bundle. Do not add this to Vercel unless you run the seed there.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
